Description: runtests.pl: fall back to getpwuid() when USER is unset;
 never substitute an undef $USER.
 .
 The Athena build container runs dpkg-buildpackage without USER, USERNAME
 or LOGNAME in the environment. runtests.pl derives $USER only from those
 variables, and runs under `use warnings FATAL => 'all'` (line 79), so at
 the first ssh-based test (582) the s/%USER/$USER/ substitution in
 subVariables() (line 3575) hits an undefined $USER and the fatal warning
 kills the whole test run ("make: Error 2") instead of skipping the test.
 .
 Two changes:
 1. Fall back to getpwuid($<) for $USER, the pure-perl equivalent of the
    `whoami` / `id -un` fallback upstream curl added in tests/servers.pm.
    With a user name available (and openssh-server installed via the
    <!nocheck> build-dependency) the sftp/scp/socks-over-ssh tests can
    actually run.
 2. Guard the %USER substitution so that if no user name can be
    determined at all, ssh-based tests skip cleanly through the existing
    "Can't start ssh server due to lack of USER name" path in
    runsshserver() rather than aborting the run.
Origin: backport, https://github.com/curl/curl (tests/servers.pm USER fallback)
Bug: https://github.com/curl/curl/issues/9007
Forwarded: not-needed (fixed differently upstream)
Author: Athena-Build
Last-Update: 2026-07-06
---
--- a/tests/runtests.pl
+++ b/tests/runtests.pl
@@ -401,6 +401,12 @@
         $USER = $ENV{LOGNAME};  # Some Unix (I think)
     }
 }
+if (!$USER) {
+    # no user name in the environment (e.g. a minimal build container);
+    # fall back to the password database. Upstream curl does the
+    # equivalent with `whoami` / `id -un` in tests/servers.pm.
+    $USER = getpwuid($<);
+}
 
 # enable memory debugging if curl is compiled with it
 $ENV{'CURL_MEMDEBUG'} = $memdump;
@@ -3572,7 +3578,12 @@
     $$thing =~ s/${prefix}FILE_PWD/$file_pwd/g;
     $$thing =~ s/${prefix}SSH_PWD/$ssh_pwd/g;
     $$thing =~ s/${prefix}SRCDIR/$srcdir/g;
-    $$thing =~ s/${prefix}USER/$USER/g;
+    # $USER may still be undefined if no user name could be determined;
+    # this script runs with FATAL warnings, so substituting undef here
+    # would abort the whole test run instead of letting ssh-based tests
+    # skip via the check in runsshserver().
+    my $subst_user = (defined $USER) ? $USER : '';
+    $$thing =~ s/${prefix}USER/$subst_user/g;
 
     $$thing =~ s/${prefix}SSHSRVMD5/$SSHSRVMD5/g;
     $$thing =~ s/${prefix}SSHSRVSHA256/$SSHSRVSHA256/g;
